#X text 240 83 A small in-memory storage with N cells. Each incoming
message is written into the corresponding memory cell and can later
be read back by sending a cell index to the last inlet \, or all cells
at once with a bang. Each cell has its own TTL counter: if the @ttl
property is greater than 0 \, every output of the cell decrements its
individual counter \, and once it reaches zero \, the cell is cleared
(when @free is on) or kept with a zero counter.;
